{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>The Urim and the Tummim.</b> It is the writing of the explicit Name, which was placed inside the folds of the breastpiece, by which He illuminates His words and perfects His words. In the Second Temple the breastpiece existed — for it is impossible for the High Priest to be lacking garments — but that Name was not inside it. And after that writing it is called מִשְׁפָּט, as it is said (Numbers 27): ״וְשָׁאַל לוֹ בְּמִשְׁפַּט הָאוּרִים״ (Yoma 73)." "<b>The judgment of the children of Israel.</b> A matter about which they are judged and instructed through it — whether to do a thing or not to do it. And according to another midrash: because the breastpiece atones for corruption of justice, it is called מִשְׁפָּט after the pardoning of judgment."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:19.944608009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}